---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Image Credits" description="Image sources and credits for Dressed in History.">
  <main class="article">
    <div class="container article-inner">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">All Stories</a>

      <header class="article-header">
        <p class="kicker">Credits</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">Image Credits</h1>
        <p class="page-deck">The photographs and archival images behind our stories.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We believe a fashion history journal should show the real thing. Wherever
          possible, we illustrate our stories with authentic historical photographs
          and archival imagery from public collections, including
          <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Images used on this site</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            CHANEL little black dress, window display —
            via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY 2.0).
          </li>
          <li>
            Closeup of a copper rivet on jeans —
            via Wikimedia Commons.
          </li>
          <li>
            Humphrey Bogart in <em>Casablanca</em> (1942) trailer still —
            via Wikimedia Commons (public domain).
          </li>
          <li>
            British officer in a trench coat, First World War —
            via Wikimedia Commons (public domain).
          </li>
          <li>
            Group at Piazza del Popolo, Rome —
            via Wikimedia Commons.
          </li>
          <li>
            Marlon Brando in <em>A Streetcar Named Desire</em> (1951) trailer still —
            via Wikimedia Commons (public domain).
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Corrections &amp; takedowns</h2>
        <p>
          If you believe an image has been credited incorrectly, or you hold rights to
          an image and would like it removed, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:hello@dressedinhistory.com">hello@dressedinhistory.com</a>
          and we will respond promptly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a href="/" class="back-link bottom">All Stories</a>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
